	amartineau@ccr.hydro.qc.ca (Alain Martineau) writes:
>I want to boot a network device from an alpha station using the MOP.
>Is it included with the base operating system or do I need DECnet ?
>I know this is not DECnet, that's why I ask, but I can't find any
>reference on this in the doc.

Get your the corresponding layered product CD for your version of
Digital UNIX.  Install DNANETMAN, DNADLI, and DNAMOP subsets from
the CD.  You don't need a PAK to enable MOP.

Use /usr/sbin/mopsetup to configure and start MOP.

