reece> ...

Thanks to everyone for the responses.  As it turns out, rz28 drives in
conjuntion with firmware version 441C have a 'known' bug which causes
the drive to spontaneously spin down.  This explains why our machine
would continue some activity (e.g., xloads, ping responses) and appear
to become gradually unresponsive.  Kudos to Jeff Finkelstein for his
superlative assistance.

Drive type and firmware version is shown at boot time, and can also be
found with scu (and probably other ways).  As root:
# file /dev/rrz*g
/dev/rrz8g:     character special (8/16390) SCSI #1 RZ28 disk #64
# scu -f /dev/rrz8g
scu> sho in
...
          Firmware Revision Level: 441C
scu> ^D
#

If anyone has more specific questions, email me directly and I'll be
happy to answer them.
