In article <3156DCC6.737E@digitronica.it>,
Andrea Mazzai  <andrea.mazzai@digitronica.it> wrote:
>Hi to everybody.
>
>How do I setup an anonymous FTP user for my Digital UNIX 3.2c Internet 
>server? I have tried with "adduser anonymous" but the system replies 
>that the name is too long - it should be 8 chars or less.

Take a look at the ftpd(8) man page - it tells how to setup anonymous
ftp (the user you want to add is "ftp", not "anonymous").  Be very careful
about which directories you have owned by the ftp user, as they can be
fiddled with by people intent on distributing pirated software.  I don't
keep a copy of passwd or group in our anonymous ftp area - it's not really
necessary unless you really want to show who owns a file, and if you put
in a real passwd file, don't leave the encrypted passwords there.  Putting
in a real passwd file could give hackers leads on accounts to try to break
in to.

Also, you might want to get a copy of the wuarchive ftpd from 
wuarchive.wustl.edu.  It has a lot of useful features for anonymous ftp
sites that will help keep your system from being used to distribute pirated
software.

