You should use MAKEDEV.

A simple way to get all the devices on your system is to shutdown your 
system, and type the following at the console:

>>> BOOT -FL "/genvmunix"

when the system boots up, type the following when logged in as root

# sizer -n fred

sizer creates a kernel configuration file that is right for the hardware 
on your system, and a MAKEDEV script called MAKEDEV.fred (I think!)

cd to /dev, and type the MAKEDEV command, and all of your devices will be 
made (including the network adaptor).

If the adaptor doesn't appear, then something is wrong.

