[ Matthew Lyle ]

| I am trying to get an external SCSI device working on my Alpha 3000/500
| running Digital Unix 3.2c but have run into some problems with getting
| the minor node correct.  I calculated a minor node number of 19458 (scsi
| bus 1, scsi address 3).  When I try to get /usr/field/diskx to test the
| disk, it fails saying that it can't open /dev/rrz10a.
|
| Any suggestions as to what I'm doing wrong with this?

Well, first of all, 19458 is the minor device number for rz11c, not rz10a.
Doing "man SCSI" will give you all the details you need to calculate these
things from the SCSI bus number, target ID, partition number, etc.  Rather
than calculate them yourself, though, an easier approach would be to just ...

        cd /dev
        ./MAKEDEV rz11

... which makes all the special files you need for that device.  (You have
to know the "NN" part of "rzNN", but the manpage tells you about that, too.)

