: disk, it fails saying that it can't open /dev/rrz10a.

: Any suggestions as to what I'm doing wrong with this?

The easiest way to make devices like disks is:

cd /dev
./MAKEDEV rz11              !11 = 8*SCSI bus + dev-ID

that gives you:

rrz11a:	character special (8/19456)
rrz11b:	character special (8/19457)
rrz11c:	character special (8/19458)
rrz11d:	character special (8/19459)
rrz11e:	character special (8/19460)
rrz11f:	character special (8/19461)
rrz11g:	character special (8/19462)
rrz11h:	character special (8/19463)
rz11a:	block special (8/19456)
rz11b:	block special (8/19457)
rz11c:	block special (8/19458)
rz11d:	block special (8/19459)
rz11e:	block special (8/19460)
rz11f:	block special (8/19461)
rz11g:	block special (8/19462)
rz11h:	block special (8/19463)

To  check out the disk device try:

file /dev/rrz11a

or use scu

