> instead have several filesets in one domain you can change
> their respective size.

There is a reason to have more than one domain. If you spread one
domain over partitions of several disks the probability that
a disk crash destroys your domain is increased. If it possible, 
I would only include partitions of one disk in a domain. The
probability that a crash of one of my disks will destroy this
domain is less, and if one of my disk crashes, only a few of
my data is affected and not all my data, as if it would happen
if I keep may data in only one large filedomain spread over
several disks.

Bye, Andy

