First check that there is enough memory in the machine, with 'swapon -s'. 
Otherwise, rebuilding the kernel is a good idea. First you must change a 
parameter in the setup, though, and I've found that changing the MAXUSER 
parameter to something higher affects quite a few other parameters as well in 
the positive direction. Do a 'man doconfig' and you will get a complete 
explanation how to rebuild the kernel.








