[ this is really more appropriate for the alt.windows.cde newsgroup ]

Your question seems a bit ambigous.  Do you mean you just want to add something
to the front panel so that when pushed the control starts an application, or
do you mean you want to embed a running X application (eg xload/xmeter) in the
front panel?  The procedure is very different (but pretty easy, in either
case) depending on which it is you wish to do.

If all you wish to do is add a new control to the front panel, then look
through your $HOME/.dt/types/dtwm.fp (if you don't have one then

	cp /usr/dt/appconfig/types/C/dtwm.fp $HOME/.dt/types/dtwm.fp

) and copy one of the Control statements in there, changing elements as
appropriate.  Note that what you specify as the PUSH_ACTION must be a valid
Dt action -- if you don't have an action yet that starts the program you wish
to start then you need to create an action using CreateAction or by editing
your own action file(s).  Check out the man page for `dtfpfile' and associated
man pages.

If you wish to embed a running X application in the front panel, then

1) arrange to have the application started when you log in, either via your
.dtprofile or via a saved session.

2) use the -name SomeNameHere  argument when starting the application.  For
example, if you wish to embed an xload in the front panel (ala HP VUE), then
when you start xload start it with (at least)

	xload -name panelload

3) add the following to your $HOME/.dt/types/dtwm.fp:

CONTROL PanelLoad
{
  TYPE              client
  CONTAINER_NAME    Top
  CONTAINER_TYPE    BOX
  POSITION_HINTS    last
  CLIENT_NAME       panelload
  CLIENT_GEOMETRY   46x46
}

the TYPE must be `client' and CLIENT_NAME must be same as was specified with
the -name argument to the X application, but change the rest as necessary.
I found it useful to add the following resources to my Dtwm resource file:

Dtwm*panelload*clientDecoration:    none
Dtwm*panelload*Label*Justify:       center

Let me know if you have questions.

Tim
