In article <6cspfa87gv.fsf@mango.atria.com> jtk@atria.com (John Kohl) writes:

John> However, on my new machine with a PCXAL keyboard, when I map the
John> <--backspace key to BackSpace, xterm sees it as DEL (although 'xev'
John> displays it properly via XLookupString as "^H").

Well, thanks to Alfred von Campe at Digital, I figured out what's going
on here.

Setting a resource
	XTerm*backspaceIsDelete:	false
or using the -/+bs, or using the Ctrl-MB2 popup menu all can be used to
correct this weird behavior.  It's apparently some new Digital-invented
xterm "feature".
