Ignore it.

It's a known problem between gcc and ld. I have been told it should be fixed
in V4.0, but I have not confirmed this. There have also been several
messages about how to fix it, but I can't confirm any of them.

But the message is harmless, caused by linking to objects with no executable
code. It does not effect the executable files in any way.
