[the question concerned using all three channels of a KZPSC-BA, vs
 collecting the disks on two channels]

If you are moving the same number of bytes through the KZPSC, I have
a hard time thinking there is much more overhead using all three
channels, and there is for sure less SCSI contention.  We have two
2100 5/250 servers (one Digital Unix and one VMS), each with a KZPSC
configured to use all three channels.  The only problems we have had
resulted from the RZ-29B firmware 7, since updated.  I would advise
you to have TWO hot spare disks if you are running RAID 5 or shadowing.

