>ian@adone.com

FUSE 2.1 runs on Digital UNIX 3.x.  FUSE V3.0 will require Digital
UNIX 4.0.  

FUSE contains an integrated set of GUI based-tools.  Many of these tools layer
on top of base operating system tools (such as make, grep, rcs).  The
tools communicate with each other, so that you can easily move from one
tool to another, for example:

1. You can go from an error in the builder to the source line on which
the error is on in the editor.

2. You can look at two revisions in the code manager and ask to see the
differences in the compare tool.

3. You can checkout the file that you are currently editing.

FUSE 2.1 consists of the following tools:
- Editors - Motif-based editor, emacs and vi
- Builder
- debugger
- man page browser
- search tool
- cross reference tool
- call graph browser
- C++ class browser 
- profiler
- code manager
- compare tool
- EnCASE tool (to integrate additional tools)
- hypertext help system

FUSE 3.0 adds the following features:
- The Porting Assistant (helps port code to Digital UNIX)
- The heap analyzer (finds memory allocation errors)
- The Program Visualizer
- The version control tool (integrates an arbitrary code management tool)
- File merge support
- CDE integration
- Tool invocation from the command line

You can get more information about FUSE on the following Web page:
http://www.digital.com/info/fuse

