Are you using KZMSAs to connect the RZ74s?

I had really bad performance problems with KZMSAs and finally upgraded
our 7000 to an 8400, partly to get  more reasonable SCSI adapters.

It took a long time to find someone in Digital that would confirm that
KZMSAs are slow; one of the problems is the maximum number of queued
I/Os--two if memory serves.  (Try doing timing dd from raw partitions
to /dev/null with several different types of adapters to see the
performance difference)

We did not find any SCSI adapters for the 7000 that 1) had a future;
2) were cost-effective and 3) had acceptable performance.

Even a KZPAA (PCI bus, Fast Narrow for about $200) has much better
performance than a KZMSA.  A KZPSA (PCI, Fast Wide) with RZ29's is
much faster :-).

Almost ANY PCI-based alpha will provide you better performance than a
7000.  Sorry.




