We have been running INN1.4 and INN1.4sec for almost three years
on Digital OSF/1.  First on OSF1.3A, later on OSF2.0, OSF3.0, and
now on OSF3.2.  The INN FAQ mentioned our machine pirates.cs.swt.edu.
Our present INN1.4sec was compiled on OSF3.0 but run on OSF3.2.
I don't think that there is a significant difference between OSF3.2
and OSF3.2D (My present machine infinite.cs.swt.edu is running
OSF3.2D-1).

On pirates.cs.swt.edu (nickname ftp.cs.swt.edu) besides the config.data
files, there is a precompiled whole package (compiled on OSF3.0). Every
file that was changed has a corresponding *.in copy saved in the
same directory.  So it's not difficult to find out the changes needed
to compile on OSF3.2D.

Hope this helps.

