In article <4h76kj$kn2@portal.gmu.edu>,
Paul D'Agostino <pdag@cybernetics.net> wrote:
>I have been searching for a single backup solution in a multi-vendor 
>environment to put some sanity and control into the process.  I've noticed 
>that OSF/1 or DigitalUnix are never among the list of possible clients.  
>The solutions I have looked at so far are: Cheyanne's ARCserve 6, 
>Palindrome's Vista, IBM's ADSTAR, and maybe one or two others.  They can 
>usually back up Ultrix, but none of them back up OSF/1.  Why?

We're using Legato Networker.  Digital distributes the server and
client for Digital Unix - the client stuff comes on the OS CD for
3.2 and up.  The server is on the Consolidated Distribution CD set.
Digital also resells Legato's Unix client kit which has client software
for SunOS, Solaris 2, SGI IRIX, and a bunch of others.  There are also
clients for Netware servers and Macs.

We're using a Alphastation 200 4/166 for the server.  We're currently
using a 8mm drive, but we have a DLT on order to replace it.  We are
backing up the following clients:  Digital Unix, Ultrix, SunOS, Solaris 2,
SGI IRIX, and HPUX.  We're going to try out the Mac client soon.

You can check out the Legato web page for more information:

  http://www.legato.com/

