In article <4hts9j$msm@nntp.Stanford.EDU>, Joshua Wai Ho Hui <wjhui@leland.Stanford.EDU> writes:
|>Hi,
|>
|>I try to compile my program which has template class declaration using
|>DEC C++ Compiler for DEC OSF. However, it always complaint that the functions
|>are not found when doing the linking.

Yes.
DEC C++ V5.1 does not support template auto-instantiation. Please
see the cxx man page for the -define_templates commandline switch.
Alternately, you could modify your source to add #pragma define_template
directives for each type of template to be instantiated.
i.e.,
   #pragma define_template sort<int>

Starting DEC C++ V5.3 (currently in field-test), template auto-instantiation
is supported.
           
Tom
