I've just tested something similar for displaying CDE on a Linux box,
and did also display the XDM login screen for a test. On the Linux box,
I logged in as root and just launched the X server:

# /usr/bin/X11/X -ac &

On the Digital UNIX side, edit /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers and add an
entry for your Linux box as if it were an X terminal, e.g.

linux.xxx.xxx:0 foreign

Then do a 'ps -ef | grep xdm' and find the pid of the parent xdm process.
Then, sending it a HUP signal causes it to reread the Xservers file and
it should startup the XDM login display.

# kill -HUP $PID

For CDE, the procedure was the same, but the file to edit is
/usr/dt/config/Xservers, and you need to find the parent dtlogin
process instead of xdm.

Other than complaints about missing DECwindows fonts, this should
work for you. Hope this helps.

Chris



